=== THE VERDICT, on the eleven rows 11 scored ===
control/parent floor (the instrument's own): worst |x/p - 1| = 0.003013
culprit/parent: min 0.85576  median 0.94103  max 0.98577
rows whose |c/p - 1| exceeds the floor: 11 of 11
rows whose |c/p - 1| exceeds 1e-3:      11 of 11
rows with FEWER instructions at the culprit: 11 of 11
rows with MORE  instructions at the culprit: 0 of 11
largest step, in units of the floor: 47.9x

WHOLE-PROCESS READING: instructions are DOWN at the culprit on EVERY scored row,
reproducibly and far outside the floor. NOT WORK-MOVED on its face -- but this is
NOT A WORK READING, and the leg says so rather than banking it: 17 % (n20000) to
96 % (n1000) of each of these counts is MKL's dsecnd() first-call clock
calibration, a WALL-TIMED busy-wait whose instruction count measures how fast that
loop's own code runs, not any work the solver does. See the pass S block below and
record_analyze.out.

THE VERDICT ITSELF IS record_analyze.out's, on the two n20000 rows where the row's own
work is the majority of the profile: with the calibration set aside INSIDE each
profile, the culprit/parent ratio reads 0.99452 and 0.99696 against a control/parent
floor of 0.99863 and 0.99980, and the three rounds' values INTERLEAVE between the two
arms. NOT WORK-MOVED: 9cebbbe's solve does not execute more instructions -- it executes
the same, to within 0.3-0.6 %, and if anything marginally fewer. 11.1's LAYOUT-MOVED
band (identical within 1e-4) is NOT reached either, so no 11.1 label is claimed.

