f7_n20000_bound_neutral/RelaxBounds             9.5305    9.7628          1.02438

THAT DIFFERENCE IS NOT TAKEN AS A MEASUREMENT, and the reason is measured, not feared.
The per-process constant is MKL's dsecnd() first-call clock calibration -- a WALL-TIMED
busy-wait (hven calls it deliberately at src/drivers/solver_init.cpp:27, through
InteriorPointSolver::ensure_solver_initialized, src/drivers/interior_point_solver.cpp:798
and :5535). Its INSTRUCTION count is not a constant: the sampled profiles put it at
2.9 e9 of an n20000 process at the same arm whose hs071 process reads 4.6 e9, and one
f7_n1000_bound_physics/MakeParameter sample read 0.9 e9. A term that moves by 5x is not
a term to subtract. reading.md 5 (iv) refused a differencing instrument for a related
reason and this leg refuses this one; what stands in its place is the PER-SYMBOL
measurement in record_analyze.out, which sets the calibration aside INSIDE each
profile and so assumes nothing about its size.

